{
  "requirement": "Marks an agent request that can still accept reusable context before adding node contents.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct ContextPhase;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.ContextPhase` is a declaration requirement. It has no MUST, MUST NOT or SHOULD clauses. Its obligation is that the SDK publicly exposes a unit marker struct, `pub struct ContextPhase;`, which labels an ask builder that can still accept context.\n\nThe requirement is tested by its `:test:` anchor, `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]`. That test checks the declaration in these ways:\n- `specified_exports` parses the inventory in `md/requirements/sdk/public-api.md`. The inventory lists `struct ContextPhase` with a declaration link to this requirement.\n- `documented_exports` walks the rustdoc HTML generated for the current source tree. For each public struct it requires an inventory declaration, so a missing or renamed `ContextPhase` fails the test. It also requires the item kind to match, so a changed kind such as a type alias would fail.\n- `check_declaration` reads the requirement's `rust,ignore` block, `pub struct ContextPhase;`. It compares that block with rustdoc's published declaration through `signature_parts`, in both directions. A change to the shape, such as adding fields, generics or members, fails the test.\n- `check_declaration` also compares trait implementations and indexed members with the requirement. A new public field or method, or a changed trait implementation, would be flagged.\n- The final inventory comparison fails on any missing or unexpected export.\n\nThe behavior the description implies is that only this state exposes `context`. That behavior is carried by other requirements: `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.agent_context`, `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.phases` and the validation-context `ask` requirement. Those requirements have their own tests and are not part of this subject. For the subject itself, a public unit struct at this path with this exact declaration is what the test enforces.\n\nI found no obligation or boundary case left untested, and no fixme acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "34070f30c190da855a0af0db8758db88cea74ad388475c8cd2f1dfaa1fb9eb00",
